        "parms": "# regexp — match and replace text\nregexp looks for a regular expression in every message. Each match leaves the third outlet, and its capture groups the second. With a substitution, the left outlet then sends the whole message with every match replaced. A message with no match leaves the right outlet as it is.\nUnlike Max, the pattern and the substitution are only set as arguments: there are no re or substitute messages. Backreferences, lookaround and \\b are not supported, and a space in a pattern is written \\s.",
